munity-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35120208511216056, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22077922158880078, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6555221, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"To summarise I feel it is beneficial to be using weaver to document/describe the signals as well as the instrumentation emitting them as they should be sharing significant amounts of data. This way the eco-system Explorer can then focus on presenting and making discoverable the emitted definitions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jack-berg** — 2025-11-10T15:29:30Z\\n\\nWhen I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nSignificantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nLater, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nSome thoughts:\\n\\n- The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\n- The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\n- The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"to summaris i feel it is benefici to be use weaver to document describ the signal a well a the instrument emit them a they should be share signific amount of data this way the eco system explor can then focus on present and make discover the emit definit jack berg 2025 11 10t15 29 30z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10 some thought the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl to generat much richer meta data that is captur by the registri today ani effort for a better registri is probabl go to requir some coordin between the repo where compon live i e sdk instrument contrib collector etc and the opentelemetri io repo some share tool can should be central in opentelemetri io but the repo should also work to do a better job of publish the type of meta data that can t be generat through simpl scanner script\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"6aef2203f67ca0d8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34394039286776856, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18181818266824085, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72222555, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-11-18T07:54:04Z\\n\\n> When I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nIt absolutely is! That's why I am in favour of this project so much. The registry has been a building block of our project from day 1, but besides a few cosmetic changes we never lifted it to a proper solution.\\n\\n> Significantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nYes 🙌 \\n\\n> Later, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nI can barely wait for it ;) \\n\\n>     * The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io?rgh-link-date=2025-11-10T15%3A29%3A30Z)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\nYes, we can learn and take from the existing schema, but overall it's insufficient. \\n\\n>     * The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\nThe registry as of today does what it was intended to do, provide a quick glance into all the things opentelemetry. but as the project evolved, the registry didn't, and as you lined out it's missing a lot of details and nuances, so this project aims to help with that. \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm 2025 11 18t07 54 04z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time it absolut is that s whi i am in favour of this project so much the registri ha been a build block of our project from day 1 but besid a few cosmet chang we never lift it to a proper solut signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather yes later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10i can bare wait for it the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io rgh link date 2025 11 10t15 3a29 3a30z but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start yes we can learn and take from the exist schema but overal it s insuffici the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri a of today doe what it wa intend to do provid a quick glanc into all the thing opentelemetri but a the project evolv the registri didn t and a you line out it s miss a lot of detail and nuanc so this project aim to help with that\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"54a7d35c2598fc15\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.33723309786776856, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18181818266824085, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6998679, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"The initial POC focused on a static-site approach which is much simpler to operate, has _almost_ no ongoing maintenance burden, and still meets our immediate needs. Personally, I'd much prefer a solution that requires as little operational overhead as possible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**trask** — 2025-10-01T19:11:49Z\\n\\n+1 on optimizing for low operational overhead since that's an area where we struggle as an Open Source project\\n\\n---\\n\\n**thompson-tomo** — 2025-10-06T05:26:18Z\\n\\nI am all for a lower operational overhead but I do get worried when I see suggestions to build something as that can create tech debt especially when it is not a key part of the organisation business/objective. Hence suggestion to use an established product.\\n\\nWith the objective of low operational effort and static site generation in mind, we should be exploring how weaver can be contribute to the solution.\\n\\nWhat I could foresee is:\\n\\n- User defines a weaver registry file which imports signals from the sem conv registry\\n\\n- User refines the imported signals based on what they are implementing\\n\\n- User defines either a seperate implementation metadata file or adds it to the registry file. TBD\\n\\n- Weaver codegen runs ie `weaver implementation generate` for the refined signals and metadata. This would produce boilerplate code which is used in the implementation and exports a yaml definition file (resolved schema).\\n\\n- the exported yaml could be added to the eco-system which is proceeded by `weaver implementation describe` to emit the static content.\\n\\nAll of that would be reusable especially if the repo/package readme could also be generated in the same manner.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-10-06T10:17:57Z\\n\\n@thompson-tomo who is a \\\"user\\\" in your example? This project is specifically aimed at creating documentation for java instrumentation (and possibly the collector and other languages as a stretch goal). There are over 250 instrumentations in the java project, and at this time none of them use weaver to define their attributes. I have experimented with introducing weaver to the project in order to generate metrics/attributes for an instrumentation, but as of this time, there are no existing plans by the SIG to rewrite everything in that repo to use weaver (that I am aware of).\\n\\nI am all for integrating weaver where it makes sense, but if we are saying we need to convert that repo to use weaver before we move ahead with this project, I fear it would be a very long time before we could deliver anything useful. There's also a significant number of things involved here that go beyond just documenting the attributes that I don't think weaver helps with.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the initi poc focus on a static site approach which is much simpler to oper ha _ almost _ no ongo mainten burden and still meet our immedi need person i d much prefer a solut that requir a littl oper overhead a possibl trask 2025 10 01t19 11 49z 1 on optim for low oper overhead sinc that s an area where we struggl a an open sourc project thompson tomo 2025 10 06t05 26 18z i am all for a lower oper overhead but i do get worri when i see suggest to build someth a that can creat tech debt especi when it is not a key part of the organis busi object henc suggest to use an establish product with the object of low oper effort and static site generat in mind we should be explor how weaver can be contribut to the solut what i could forese is user defin a weaver registri file which import signal from the sem conv registri user refin the import signal base on what they are implement user defin either a seper implement metadata file or add it to the registri file tbd weaver codegen run ie weaver implement generat for the refin signal and metadata this would produc boilerpl code which is use in the implement and export a yaml definit file resolv schema the export yaml could be ad to the eco system which is proceed by weaver implement describ to emit the static content all of that would be reusabl especi if the repo packag readm could also be generat in the same manner jaydeluca 2025 10 06t10 17 57z thompson tomo who is a user in your exampl this project is specif aim at creat document for java instrument and possibl the collector and other languag a a stretch goal there are over 250 instrument in the java project and at this time none of them use weaver to defin their attribut i have experi with introduc weaver to the project in order to generat metric attribut for an instrument but a of this time there are no exist plan by the sig to rewrit everyth in that repo to use weaver that i am awar of i am all for integr weaver where it make sens but if we are say we need to convert that repo to use weaver befor we move ahead with this project i fear it would be a veri long time befor we could deliv anyth use there s also a signific number of thing involv here that go beyond just document the attribut that i don t think weaver help with\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"99d77b00ebd65a06\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3357386178677686, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.18181818266824085, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6948863, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```suggestion\\n\\n* @svrnm (Severin Neumann)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T12:00:51Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n* @jaydeluca (Grafana Labs)\\n\\n* @svrnm (Causely)\\n\\n* Looking for other leads with experience in OpenTelemetry instrumentation and/or web application development\\n\\n```\\n\\nI am happy to assist the project to get up to speed, but overall it would be a great opportunity to step up as lead.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` (line 205) — 2025-09-19T12:01:36Z\\n\\nWe might think about other projects outside of OpenTelemetry that would be interested in consuming this data, e.g. I could imagine that Backstage and similar projects could make use of this data. \\n\\n**mx-psi** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` — 202