83\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.38131873305761316, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.25925926008230454, \"vector_similarity\": 0.66612417, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Meeting notes: [Ecosystem Explorer Project](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1QBpFmSR54fGus8q6RraUj0-mEjSoX7S7fdlgsvxZsuk/edit?usp=sharing)  \\n\\n  - [https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml](https://github.com/mikeblum/otel-explorer-go-docs/blob/3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0/instrumentation-list.yaml)  \\n\\n### SIG Security: release signing\\n\\n- Robert proposed enabling GitHub “signature releases” in addition to existing tag signing and GPG signatures of source archives.\\n\\n- Key points:\\n\\n  - GitHub’s source tarball/zip is generated at download time; signing artifacts strengthens trust and mitigates changes over time.\\n\\n  - Double-signing is acceptable and beneficial for OSS Scorecard/compliance.\\n\\n  - Constraint: Artifacts must be uploaded at release time; cannot regenerate later.\\n\\n- Decision: Proceed with enabling signature releases; update release documentation and ensure process discipline.\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164](https://github.com/open-telemetry/sig-security/issues/164)  \\n\\n### KubeCon updates\\n\\n- OpenTelemetry Observatory booth confirmed.\\n\\n- Go SIG will meet at the booth (Tuesday morning, local time; check published schedule).\\n\\n- Plan to cancel the Zoom SIG meeting during KubeCon week; reminder will be sent next week.\\n\\n- Community encouraged to stop by the booth and participate.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-06]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479655348  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:39:04Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:40:01Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-30\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n- Tyler Yahn\\n\\n- Bryan Boreham\\n\\n- Damien Mathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"meet note ecosystem explor project http doc googl com document d 1qbpfmsr54fgus8q6rrauj0 mejsox7s7fdlgsvxzsuk edit usp share http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml http github com mikeblum otel explor go doc blob 3797539be4f5a760e99586c0de72496019f5e6b0 instrument list yaml sig secur releas sign robert propos enabl github signatur releas in addit to exist tag sign and gpg signatur of sourc archiv key point github s sourc tarbal zip is generat at download time sign artifact strengthen trust and mitig chang over time doubl sign is accept and benefici for os scorecard complianc constraint artifact must be upload at releas time can not regener later decis proceed with enabl signatur releas updat releas document and ensur process disciplin refer http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 http github com open telemetri sig secur issu 164 kubecon updat opentelemetri observatori booth confirm go sig will meet at the booth tuesday morn local time check publish schedul plan to cancel the zoom sig meet dure kubecon week remind will be sent next week communiti encourag to stop by the booth and particip sourc id src note 06 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479655348 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 39 04z updat 2025 11 03t09 40 01z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 30 attende tyler yahn bryan boreham damien mathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3702667240576132, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.25925926008230454, \"vector_similarity\": 0.62928414, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-09-19T12:39:50Z\\n\\n>  guess my concern is with the naming, maybe something like \\\"Ecosystem Documentation\\\", and \\\"Ecosystem explorer\\\" would make people think that the Collector is (potentially) included, the current naming seems more focused on language libraries\\n\\nAh yes, that makes sense, I can update. Thanks @mx-psi \\n\\n---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-09-19T14:26:38Z\\n\\n@jaydeluca can you add a section about the existing registry, how this project and the registry are related to each other, for me it would be totally fine to say that this is going to replace the registry eventually.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**thompson-tomo** — 2025-10-01T03:14:12Z\\n\\nSo I have come here from the comment in the backstage channel.\\n\\nThinking about this what are the thoughts about building a backstage plugin to add support for open telemetry in a similar fashion to api's (https://github.com/backstage/backstage/blob/master/plugins/api-docs/README.md). We could then use backstage rather than building a tool for the ecosystem explorer.\\n\\nI would see the development steps as being:\\n\\n- introducing the telemetry section to list the signals and show the definitions in backstage\\n\\n- Allow components (libraries) to define what signals they produce and link it to the definition just like they can for apis.\\n\\n- Provide a way to show technology specific docs ie oracledb which provides descriptive info and the corresponding signals.\\n\\nI also think it would be beneficial to ensure that weaver can be used to generate the file to add to the ecosystem Explorer so that as a user has one tool to use.\\n\\nA nice thing I forsee is that we could potentially focus the sem conv specification section of the website on defining the base signals and the informative info is captured in the eco system Explorer.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-10-01T19:08:52Z\\n\\n> Thinking about this what are the thoughts about building a backstage plugin to add support for open telemetry in a similar fashion to api's (https://github.com/backstage/backstage/blob/master/plugins/api-docs/README.md). We could then use backstage rather than building a tool for the ecosystem explorer.\\n\\nThanks for raising this @thompson-tomo, it is something we also considered and explored a bit.\\n\\nI think the main concern is the tradeoff in complexity. Backstage brings a lot of functionality, but it also requires provisioning infrastructure, ongoing upgrades, and database maintenance. In my experience, it often needs a dedicated team to keep it running smoothly. For our use case, much of that extra functionality isn't really essential, and could actually slow us down.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"jaydeluca 2025 09 19t12 39 50z guess my concern is with the name mayb someth like ecosystem document and ecosystem explor would make peopl think that the collector is potenti includ the current name seem more focus on languag librari ah yes that make sens i can updat thank mx psi svrnm 2025 09 19t14 26 38z jaydeluca can you add a section about the exist registri how this project and the registri are relat to each other for me it would be total fine to say that this is go to replac the registri eventu thompson tomo 2025 10 01t03 14 12z so i have come here from the comment in the backstag channel think about this what are the thought about build a backstag plugin to add support for open telemetri in a similar fashion to api s http github com backstag backstag blob master plugin api doc readm md we could then use backstag rather than build a tool for the ecosystem explor i would see the develop step a be introduc the telemetri section to list the signal and show the definit in backstag allow compon librari to defin what signal they produc and link it to the definit just like they can for api provid a way to show technolog specif doc ie oracledb which provid descript info and the correspond signal i also think it would be benefici to ensur that weaver can be use to generat the file to add to the ecosystem explor so that a a user ha one tool to use a nice thing i forse is that we could potenti focus the sem conv specif section of the websit on defin the base signal and the inform info is captur in the eco system explor jaydeluca 2025 10 01t19 08 52z think about this what are the thought about build a backstag plugin to add support for open telemetri in a similar fashion to api s http github com backstag backstag blob master plugin api doc readm md we could then use backstag rather than build a tool for the ecosystem explor thank for rais this thompson tomo it is someth we also consid and explor a bit i think the main concern is the tradeoff in complex backstag bring a lot of function but it also requir provis infrastructur ongo upgrad and databas mainten in my experi it often need a dedic team to keep it run smooth for our use case much of that extra function isn t realli essenti and could actual slow u down\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"ca55cff066dc41c3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32080463536625514, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72366977, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"> Is the Collector intentionally out of scope? From the discussions I have had with @svrnm it seems like this should be similar enough (instead of libraries we would be talking about components), so I feel like it would be a good idea to include it as well\\n\\n@mx-psi yes and no. It's not _entirely_ left out of the scope (see [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000/files#diff-9f98d0309d3d9caafc8b541e0eb2fe512726fecb18f94a4d0831952c6b29a2d4R102-R105)), I have added evaluating the feasibility of this approach for both the collector and javascript as within scope, but I personally cannot commit to doing all the legwork for those as well. If we were to commit to a more concrete deliverable for those two projects, I think we will need a larger team.\\n\\nDo you think the language I used around this isn't clear, or do you think it should be changed?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**mx-psi** — 2025-09-19T12:38:35Z\\n\\n> > Is the Collector intentionally out of scope? From the discussions I have had with @svrnm it seems like this should be similar enough (instead of libraries we would be talking about components), so I feel like it would be a good idea to include it as well\\n\\n> \\n\\n> @mx-psi yes and no. It's not _entirely_ left out of the scope (see [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000/files#diff-9f98d0309d3d9caafc8b541e0eb2fe512726fecb18f94a4d0831952c6b29a2d4R102-R105)), I have added evaluating the feasibility of this approach for both the collector and javascript as within scope, but I personally cannot commit to doing all the legwork for those as well. If we were to commit to a more concrete deliverable for those two projects, I think we will need a larger team.\\n\\n> \\n\\n> Do you think the language I used around this isn't clear, or do you think it should be changed?\\n\\nI guess my concern is with the naming, maybe something like \\\"Ecosystem Documentation\\\", and \\\"Ecosystem explorer\\\" would make people think that the Collector is (potentially) included, the current naming seems more focused on language libraries\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"is the collector intent out of scope from the discuss i have had with svrnm it seem like this should be similar enough instead of librari we would be talk about compon so i feel like it would be a good idea to includ it a well mx psi yes and no it s not _ entir _ left out of the scope see here http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 file diff 9f98d0309d3d9caafc8b541e0eb2fe512726fecb18f94a4d0831952c6b29a2d4r102 r105 i have ad evalu the feasibl of this approach for both the collector and javascript a within scope but i person can not commit to do all the legwork for those a well if we were to commit to a more concret deliver for those two project i think we will need a larger team do you think the languag i use around this isn t clear or do you think it should be chang mx psi 2025 09 19t12 38 35z is the collector intent out of scope from the discuss i have had with svrnm it seem like this should be similar enough instead of librari we would be talk about compon so i feel like it would be a good idea to includ it a well mx psi yes and no it s not _ entir _ left out of the scope see here http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 file diff 9f98d0309d3d9caafc8b541e0eb2fe512726fecb18f94a4d0831952c6b29a2d4r102 r105 i have ad evalu the feasibl of this approach for both the collector and javascript a within scope but i person can not commit to do all the legwork for those a well if we were to commit to a more concret deliver for those two project i think we will need a larger team do you think the languag i use around this isn t clear or do you think it should be chang i guess my concern is with the name mayb someth like ecosystem document and ecosystem explor would make peopl think that the collector is potenti includ the current name seem more focus on languag librari\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"08d9e72931d67240\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3124319593662551, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69576085, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"To summarise I feel it is beneficial to be using weaver to document/describe the signals as well as the instrumentation emitting them as they should be sharing significant amounts of data. This way the eco-system Explorer can then focus on presenting and making discoverable the emitted definitions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jack-berg** — 2025-11-10T15:29:30Z\\n\\nWhen I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nSignificantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nLater, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nSome thoughts:\\n\\n- The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\n- The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\n- The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"to summaris i feel it is benefici to be use weaver to document describ the signal a well a the instrument emit them a they should be share signific amount of data this way the eco system explor can then focus on present and make discover the emit definit jack berg 2025 11 10t15 29 30z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10 some thought the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl to generat much richer meta data that is captur by the registri today ani effort for a better registri is probabl go to requir some coordin between the repo where compon live i e sdk instrument contrib collector etc and the opentelemetri io repo some share tool can should be central in opentelemetri io but the repo should also work to do a better job of publish the type of meta data that can t be generat through simpl scanner script\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"6aef2203f67ca0d8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31193006236625515, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1481481490946502, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69408786, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 50, \"total_pages\": 5}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"\\\"Ecosystem Explorer\\\" implementation \\\"delivered\\\"\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
