**: area/project-proposal  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (16)\\n\\n**jaydeluca** — 2025-09-19T12:34:33Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston descript this pr contain a project propos for a new standalon ecosystem explor document websit poc can be seen here http jaydeluca github io instrument explor note this project propos is depend on identifi collabor for the staf bit we will use this project propos doc to social the effort in hope of find peopl interest in particip relat http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io issu 7740 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri java instrument issu 13468 http github com org open telemetri project 153 queri sort 3aupdated desc is 3aopen sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston discuss 16 jaydeluca 2025 09 19t12 34 33z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"3dcb1276c9ec6d03\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3801441928338428, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20956971833406124, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7781513, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**svrnm** — COMMENTED — 2025-11-20T18:33:12Z\\n\\n**svrnm** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:18:34Z\\n\\n**trask** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T19:24:07Z\\n\\n**maryliag** — APPROVED — 2025-11-20T20:54:14Z\\n\\n**mx-psi** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T10:32:49Z\\n\\n**jack-berg** — APPROVED — 2025-11-21T15:57:47Z\\n\\n**tedsuo** — APPROVED — 2025-12-01T18:24:54Z\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-02]\\n\\n# Pull Request: Project Proposal: Ecosystem Explorer (open-telemetry/community#3000)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/community/pull/3000  \\n\\n**Author**: jaydeluca  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-09-19T10:11:57Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-02T08:40:24Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: merged (2025-12-01T19:04:18Z)  \\n\\n**Branch**: `instrumentation-docs` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +251 / -0 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: area/project-proposal  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review Comments (13)\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:58:43Z\\n\\nPersonally I would put the extraction and availability of the meta data first, and the web application second. There might be other places&tools where people would want to have that data available.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:42Z\\n\\neven if it would be a small one, I think having a dedicated SIG which is populated from Java&Comms and some other SIGs would be the way forward, and provide clear ownership.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T11:59:55Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"svrnm comment 2025 11 20t18 33 12z svrnm approv 2025 11 20t19 18 34z trask approv 2025 11 20t19 24 07z maryliag approv 2025 11 20t20 54 14z mx psi approv 2025 11 21t10 32 49z jack berg approv 2025 11 21t15 57 47z tedsuo approv 2025 12 01t18 24 54z sourc id src pr 02 pull request project propos ecosystem explor open telemetri communiti 3000 canon url http github com open telemetri communiti pull 3000 author jaydeluca creat 2025 09 19t10 11 57z updat 2025 12 02t08 40 24z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state merg 2025 12 01t19 04 18z branch instrument doc main chang 251 0 across 2 file label area project propos mileston review comment 13 svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 58 43z person i would put the extract and avail of the meta data first and the web applic second there might be other place tool where peopl would want to have that data avail svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 42z even if it would be a small one i think have a dedic sig which is popul from java comm and some other sig would be the way forward and provid clear ownership svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t11 59 55z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"d1c12561e10f79e0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34647396574610945, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16942213678015636, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7595949, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"To summarise I feel it is beneficial to be using weaver to document/describe the signals as well as the instrumentation emitting them as they should be sharing significant amounts of data. This way the eco-system Explorer can then focus on presenting and making discoverable the emitted definitions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**jack-berg** — 2025-11-10T15:29:30Z\\n\\nWhen I read this proposal, I see this project as a an attempt to build a new registry (registry 2.0). I'm very supportive of this as I've been complaining about various deficiencies of the registry for some time.\\n\\nSignificantly, the proposal is to launch the new effort in parallel to the existing registry, allowing the contributors to iterate quickly and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gathering.\\n\\nLater, once we've worked out the sharp edges, we can merge registry 1.0 into registry 2.0, and EOL registry 1.0.\\n\\nSome thoughts:\\n\\n- The registry already has a data model for capturing meta data about components (schema [here](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io)), but its insufficient. As you note, there's all sorts of data which is important to capture and visualize for end users, which as of now, is very difficult for users to discover. The key examples being: configuration schema, schema of telemetry emitted, instructions on how to get started.\\n\\n- The [registry](https://opentelemetry.io/ecosystem/registry/) already has tools for searching for components, and displaying bits of information about them, but its insufficient. More than anything else, the registry is an index of links, requiring the user to follow the link and find installation / configuration / telemetry schema details in the linked website / repository. Except this information is no always available, and when it is, there's no standardization about the display. A richer registry schema would allow a richer / more useful visualization experience.\\n\\n- The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"to summaris i feel it is benefici to be use weaver to document describ the signal a well a the instrument emit them a they should be share signific amount of data this way the eco system explor can then focus on present and make discover the emit definit jack berg 2025 11 10t15 29 30z when i read this propos i see this project a a an attempt to build a new registri registri 20 i m veri support of this a i ve been complain about various defici of the registri for some time signific the propos is to launch the new effort in parallel to the exist registri allow the contributor to iter quick and avoid the friction of a bunch of up front data model design work and consensus gather later onc we ve work out the sharp edg we can merg registri 10 into registri 20 and eol registri 10 some thought the registri alreadi ha a data model for captur meta data about compon schema here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io but it insuffici a you note there s all sort of data which is import to captur and visual for end user which a of now is veri difficult for user to discov the key exampl be configur schema schema of telemetri emit instruct on how to get start the registri http opentelemetri io ecosystem registri alreadi ha tool for search for compon and display bit of inform about them but it insuffici more than anyth els the registri is an index of link requir the user to follow the link and find instal configur telemetri schema detail in the link websit repositori except this inform is no alway avail and when it is there s no standard about the display a richer registri schema would allow a richer more use visual experi the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl to generat much richer meta data that is captur by the registri today ani effort for a better registri is probabl go to requir some coordin between the repo where compon live i e sdk instrument contrib collector etc and the opentelemetri io repo some share tool can should be central in opentelemetri io but the repo should also work to do a better job of publish the type of meta data that can t be generat through simpl scanner script\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"6aef2203f67ca0d8\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3370219381046621, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15402012443523164, \"vector_similarity\": 0.76402617, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \">     * The registry already has [tooling](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry.io/blob/main/scripts/registry-scanner/index.mjs?rgh-link-date=2025-11-10T15%3A29%3A30Z) for scanning for project repositories and creating / updating registry component entries. The problem is, its all centralized in the `opentelemetry.io` project and standardized, meaning that its only possible to scrape the types of meta data which can scraped from a central script. In his prototype, @jaydeluca has built tooling which leverages domain knowledge specific to the `opentelemetry-java-instrumentation` project, and is therefore able to generate much richer meta data that is captured by the registry today. Any effort for a better registry is probably going to require some coordination between the repos where components live (i.e SDK, instrumentation, contrib, collector, etc) and the `opentelemetry.io` repo. Some shared tooling can / should be centralized in `opentelemetry.io`, but the repos should also work to do a better job of publishing the types of meta data that can't be generated through simple scanner scripts.\\n\\nThose scripts (like most moving pieces of the registry) are hotfixes and bandage, so having having dedicated tooling and people taking care of it, is part of this proposal. I don't think it necessarily belongs into the dotio repo, in my mind we would have a repository who holds all the tooling to crawl that data and makes it accessible to consumers like opentelemetrydotio, but maybe others as well (think https://artifacthub.io/, backstage, CLI tools, etc.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n**thompson-tomo** — 2025-11-30T14:38:07Z\\n\\nAs another thought have we considered leveraging [artifact hub](https://artifacthub.io/) from the cncf and potentially just embedding an open telemetry collector plugin category as mentioned is possible in https://artifacthub.io/docs/topics/embedding_artifacts/\\n\\n---\\n\\n**svrnm** — 2025-12-01T08:20:26Z\\n\\n> As another thought have we considered leveraging [artifact hub](https://artifacthub.io/) from the cncf and potentially just embedding an open telemetry collector plugin category as mentioned is possible in [artifacthub.io/docs/topics/embedding_artifacts](https://artifacthub.io/docs/topics/embedding_artifacts/)\\n\\nYes, we have considered that, it's one of the potential upstream receivers of this project. \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"the registri alreadi ha tool http github com open telemetri opentelemetri io blob main script registri scanner index mjs rgh link date 2025 11 10t15 3a29 3a30z for scan for project repositori and creat updat registri compon entri the problem is it all central in the opentelemetri io project and standard mean that it onli possibl to scrape the type of meta data which can scrape from a central script in his prototyp jaydeluca ha built tool which leverag domain knowledg specif to the opentelemetri java instrument project and is therefor abl t