: \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"id\": \"0032f870da180d9a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3251607421046621, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15402012443523164, \"vector_similarity\": 0.72448885, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"874039c68a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479655348.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 7597, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:24\", \"token_count\": 1926, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```suggestion\\n\\n* @svrnm (Severin Neumann)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` — 2025-09-19T12:00:51Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n* @jaydeluca (Grafana Labs)\\n\\n* @svrnm (Causely)\\n\\n* Looking for other leads with experience in OpenTelemetry instrumentation and/or web application development\\n\\n```\\n\\nI am happy to assist the project to get up to speed, but overall it would be a great opportunity to step up as lead.\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/instrumentation-documentation.md` (line 205) — 2025-09-19T12:01:36Z\\n\\nWe might think about other projects outside of OpenTelemetry that would be interested in consuming this data, e.g. I could imagine that Backstage and similar projects could make use of this data. \\n\\n**mx-psi** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` — 2025-10-29T12:16:22Z\\n\\nI think we can list the Collector SIG here as well\\n\\n**mx-psi** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` (line 179) — 2025-10-29T12:16:48Z\\n\\nI'd be happy to be listed as part of the Collector staffing\\n\\n**vitorvasc** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` (line 197) — 2025-10-30T15:07:24Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n* @jaydeluca (Jay DeLuca - Grafana Labs) - Java ecosystem\\n\\n* @vitorvasc (Vitor Vasconcellos - Mercado Libre)  \\n\\n```\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` — 2025-11-18T07:55:05Z\\n\\nbased on the discussions we had, I think this is no longer entirely true?\\n\\n**svrnm** on `projects/ecosystem-explorer.md` — 2025-11-18T07:58:54Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n1. Metadata Format Definition (Collaborative dependency)\\n\\n```\\n\\n\\\"out of scope\\\" might not be the right term here, it's not the primary purpose of the project, and as you have outlined below the goal is to use what exists or to **collaborate** with SIGs as they define their own. \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"suggest svrnm severin neumann svrnm on project instrument document md 2025 09 19t12 00 51z suggest jaydeluca grafana lab svrnm caus look for other lead with experi in opentelemetri instrument and or web applic develop i am happi to assist the project to get up to speed but overal it would be a great opportun to step up a lead svrnm on project instrument document md line 205 2025 09 19t12 01 36z we might think about other project outsid of opentelemetri that would be interest in consum this data e g i could imagin that backstag and similar project could make use of this data mx psi on project ecosystem explor md 2025 10 29t12 16 22z i think we can list the collector sig here a well mx psi on project ecosystem explor md line 179 2025 10 29t12 16 48z i d be happi to be list a part of the collector staf vitorvasc on project ecosystem explor md line 197 2025 10 30t15 07 24z suggest jaydeluca jay deluca grafana lab java ecosystem vitorvasc vitor vasconcello mercado libr svrnm on project ecosystem explor md 2025 11 18t07 55 05z base on the discuss we had i think this is no longer entir true svrnm on project ecosystem explor md 2025 11 18t07 58 54z suggest 1 metadata format definit collabor depend out of scope might not be the right term here it s not the primari purpos of the project and a you have outlin below the goal is to use what exist or to collabor with sig a they defin their own\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"id\": \"4b14ba696e7f6783\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3209061848217676, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12321609974538227, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78218305, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875a6c568a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/community-3000.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 25436, \"chunk_count\": 14, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:58\", \"token_count\": 7169, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-16T07:44:04Z\\n\\nI created \\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6904\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6903\\n\\nI think it might be also good to add some \\\"error recording\\\" recommendations in https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, we should first clarify it on the semantic conventions side.\\n\\n>  I believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nThis seems not compliant with https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-metrics\\n\\n> Errors that were retried or handled (allowing an operation to complete gracefully) SHOULD NOT be recorded on spans or metrics that describe this operation.\\n\\nCurrently, the only use case I see the only use of `span.RecordError` to use it for \\\"unhandled exceptions\\\" (which for Go can be done in the SDK) and to record multiple errors like here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go#L119-L124\\n\\nI do not find the semantic conventions clear and probably some work is also needed there.\\n\\nCC @lmolkova\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-03T20:45:58Z\\n\\nSorry for joining the discussion late.\\n\\n@pellared I am confused about what we should do to handle errors, especially **non-terminating errors**. Should we do nothing if we encounter an error?\\n\\nFor instance, when facing code like this, do we do nothing for the error we receive?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"pellar 2025 06 16t07 44 04z i creat http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6904 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6903 i think it might be also good to add some error record recommend in http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev we should first clarifi it on the semant convent side i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error this seem not compliant with http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on metric error that were retri or handl allow an oper to complet grace should not be record on span or metric that describ this oper current the onli use case i see the onli use of span recorderror to use it for unhandl except which for go can be done in the sdk and to record multipl error like here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob 9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go l119 l124 i do not find the semant convent clear and probabl some work is also need there cc lmolkova xsam 2025 08 03t20 45 58z sorri for join the discuss late pellar i am confus about what we should do to handl error especi non termin error should we do noth if we encount an error for instanc when face code like this do we do noth for the error we receiv go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"edc3ac974ee2a669\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31894209346321484, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13861811209030694, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73969805, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f19